Search clang's compiler headers before GCC's own in clang-tidy

clang-tidy gets the compile command of the C++ toolchain in use. A hermetic
GCC toolchain passes -nostdinc and lists GCC's own compiler headers,
lib/gcc/<target>/<version>/include, whose intrinsics headers call GCC
builtins that clang lacks. Any source that includes <immintrin.h> then fails
to lint with clang-diagnostic-error.

This moves that directory to the end in _safe_flags, as -idirafter, and turns
-nostdinc into -nostdlibinc, so clang-tidy finds its own compiler headers
before GCC's. Flags without GCC's directory are left as they are.

The runtime part of https://github.com/aspect-build/rules_lint/pull/1045
(its unit test is left out). Drop this patch once a release carries it.

